# [Count Subarrays With Loose Bounds](https://leetcode.com/problems/count-subarrays-with-loose-bounds/)

## Approach
- Use two pointers, `left` and `right`, to track the current valid segment.
- If an element is smaller than `minK` or greater than `maxK`, move `left` to the next position after the invalid element.
- For every valid element, add `(right - left + 1)` to the answer, representing all subarrays ending at the current index within the valid segment.

## Code
```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    long long countSubarrays(vector<int>& nums, int minK, int maxK) {
        long long ans = 0;
        int left = 0, right = 0, n = nums.size();

        while (right < n) {
            while (right < n && 
                  (nums[right] < minK || nums[right] > maxK)) {
                right++;
                left = right;
            }

            if (right < n && nums[right] <= maxK && nums[right] >= minK) {
                ans += (right - left + 1);
            }

            right++;
        }

        return ans;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis
- **Time Complexity:** \(O(n)\), as each element is visited at most a constant number of times.
- **Space Complexity:** \(O(1)\), as only a few variables are used.

